{"id":"gifts-near-contract-start","title":"Gifts and paid travel reported within 90 days of a contract start between the giver and the filer’s department","tier":"CLEARED","question":"When an official or employee reports a gift from a company or nonprofit that holds a contract with their own department, does the gift fall close to the start of a contract?","finding":"126 reported gifts and travel payments come from a giver that holds, at some time, a contract with the filer’s own department. For 27 of them a contract between the two began within 90 days of the gift; moving every gift one year earlier or later gives 24, so gifts are no closer to contract starts than the calendar alone gives. The largest is a travel payment worth $5,124 from San Francisco AIDS Foundation to a filer in EOBCDH_Public Health Commission on 2018-07-22; contract 1000009852: HIV Testing ($930,317) began on 2018-07-01.","how":"Gifts and travel are Form 700 Schedules D and E with amended copies removed. The giver is matched by exact name (after removing punctuation and company suffixes) to the prime contractor of a contract in the City’s contract table held by a department the filer’s department name maps to, using the department table of the “gifts vs payments” analysis. The nearest contract start date is taken; “days” is the start date minus the gift date. The comparison repeats the count with each gift moved 365 days each way, which keeps the season (many contracts start on 1 July, many gifts come in December). Supervisors and mayors are left to the next screen. Filers are shown by position and department, not by name.","limits":"The contract table gives a term start, not the day the award was decided or signed, and it has no amendments’ dates. A gift from a contractor may be an event ticket, a conference fee from a professional body, or a gift to the department reported by its head. Whether a gift came from a restricted source, and whether the filer took part in the contract, is not in these files; each row is a question for the department. Public bodies as givers are left out.","columns":[{"k":"position","t":"Filer’s position","type":"text"},{"k":"department","t":"Department","type":"text"},{"k":"org","t":"Giver","type":"org"},{"k":"kind","t":"Kind","type":"text"},{"k":"amount","t":"Value","type":"usd"},{"k":"given","t":"Date","type":"date"},{"k":"what","t":"As reported","type":"text"},{"k":"contract","t":"Contract with the department","type":"text"},{"k":"agreed","t":"Agreed amount","type":"usd"},{"k":"started","t":"Term start","type":"date"},{"k":"days","t":"Days from gift to start","type":"days"}],"rows":[{"position":"Commissioner","department":"EOBCDH_Public Health Commission","org":"San Francisco AIDS Foundation","orgKey":"SAN FRANCISCO AIDS FOUNDATION","kind":"travel payment","amount":5124,"given":"2018-07-22","what":"Amsterdam, Netherlands","contract":"1000009852: HIV Testing","agreed":930317,"started":"2018-07-01","days":-21},{"position":"General Manager","department":"EOBCDH_Recreation and Park Department","org":"San Francisco Parks Alliance","orgKey":"SAN FRANCISCO PARKS ALLIANCE","kind":"travel payment","amount":622,"given":"2019-09-11","what":"Seattle, WA","contract":"1000015887: REC-Ward-McLaren Budget","agreed":25000,"started":"2019-09-09","days":-2},{"position":"Commissioner","department":"EOBCDH_Aging & Adult Services Commission","org":"Shanti Project","orgKey":"SHANTI PROJECT","kind":"gift","amount":450,"given":"2019-10-03","what":"Annual Gala","contract":"1000017438: Care Navigation and Peer Suppo","agreed":2465977,"started":"2020-01-01","days":90},{"position":"Executive Director","department":"EOBCDH_Environment Department on the","org":"Community Initiatives","orgKey":"COMMUNITY INITIATIVES","kind":"gift","amount":318,"given":"2018-06-13","what":"Regeneration Project Event Ticket","contract":"1000012461: ENV.FriendsSFE.Clim-ToxInterns","agreed":9890,"started":"2018-09-01","days":80},{"position":"Policy Division--All staff","depar